  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "The Mental Model: Reading Git History",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading Git History",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "History is a DAG of snapshots, not a timeline. Each commit points at its parent(s)."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "HEAD",
              "main",
              "C3",
              "C2",
              "C1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Commit = snapshot + parent + author + message",
            "`git log` walks commits reachable from HEAD",
            "SHA = hash of content, not of change intent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Author vs Committer",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Author: who wrote the change",
            "Committer: who applied it",
            "Diverges after rebase or cherry-pick"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Branches vs Reflog",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Branches",
            "Reflog"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "What",
              "editable labels",
              "real HEAD moves"
            ],
            [
              "Pushed?",
              "yes",
              "never"
            ],
            [
              "Role",
              "public story",
              "local trail"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ask first: introduced X? wrote line Y? where did content go?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# the everyday map view",
            "git log --oneline --graph --all",
            "# compact fields for notes",
            "git log --format='%h %an %ad %s'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Same change ≠ same SHA",
          "text": "Timestamps and parents differ, so a cherry-pick always gets a new hash. Content-addressing keys on data, not intent."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Tool Cheat-Sheet",
          "items": [
            "bisect → which commit broke it",
            "blame → who touched this line",
            "`-S` → when did content change",
            "reflog → recover anything local"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Log Searching",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git log --grep='timeout' --all -i",
            "git log --author='ana' --since=2024-01",
            "git log --since=2024-01 -- path/file.c",
            "git log --grep='fix' --grep='seg' --all-match"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--grep` filters messages, `--all` = every branch",
            "`-i` makes matching case-insensitive",
            "multiple `--grep`: OR, `--all-match`: AND"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "git log Searching: Messages, Diffs, Authors",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Diff-Level Search",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`-p` full patch, `--stat` files touched, `-<n>` limit",
            "`-G'regex'` matches diff lines",
            "`-S'string'` quick pickaxe inline",
            "`-L :func:file` traces one function",
            "`--follow` tracks renames (per-file only)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Searches",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`--grep`",
              "messages",
              "cheapest"
            ],
            [
              "`-G`",
              "diff text",
              "regex"
            ],
            [
              "`-L`",
              "line range",
              "evolution"
            ],
            [
              "`--follow`",
              "path",
              "renames"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Filter cheap first",
          "text": "Shrink the candidate set with pathspec and `--since` before running expensive `-G`/`-S` over every commit."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Format Fields",
          "items": [
            "`%h` short SHA",
            "`%an` author",
            "`%ad` date",
            "`%s` subject"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "When did this function last change?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Trace the range, not the file",
            "Clearer than blame for evolution"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "git log -p -L :parse_url:src/net.c"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "git blame",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`git blame <file>` prints SHA, author, date per line — the LAST commit that changed it, not the original idea."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git blame -L 10,25 -w -C src/app.py",
            "git show <sha>   # full commit context"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cut the Noise",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`-w` ignore whitespace-only edits",
            "`-C` detect copies from other files",
            "`-M` detect moves within the file",
            "list sweeps in `.git-blame-ignore-revs`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Ignores"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`-w`",
              "whitespace"
            ],
            [
              "`-C`",
              "cross-file moves"
            ],
            [
              "`-M`",
              "in-file moves"
            ],
            [
              "`--ignore-rev`",
              "one listed SHA"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cost & Limits",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "O(lines × history) on long-lived files",
            "range-limit: `git blame v2.0..HEAD -- file`",
            "follows current path — renamed? use old path",
            "`--line-porcelain` for scripts/editors"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Last touch ≠ original intent",
          "text": "A reformat commit can steal the blame. Check `-w -C` and ignore-revs before accusing the author."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "GUI Extras",
          "items": [
            "VS Code: Toggle Blame Annotations",
            "GitHub Blame: per-line + side diffs"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Suspect line — now what?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "blame with `-w -C`",
            "copy the SHA",
            "read the whole commit"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "git blame -w -C file",
            "git show <sha>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "git bisect: Binary Search for Bugs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "git bisect",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Binary search over history: O(log n) test runs to isolate one bad commit."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "good",
              "mid?",
              "half",
              "mid?",
              "culprit"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git bisect start",
            "git bisect bad HEAD",
            "git bisect good v1.0",
            "git bisect run make test"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Git checks out the midpoint each round",
            "exit 0 = good, non-zero = bad",
            "exit 125 = skip, can't test this one"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Session Control",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`skip` → results may turn approximate",
            "`log` saves, `replay` re-runs later",
            "`visualize` shows remaining candidates",
            "always `reset` when done"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Role"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`run <cmd>`",
              "automate testing"
            ],
            [
              "`skip`",
              "untestable commit"
            ],
            [
              "`log`/`replay`",
              "save session"
            ],
            [
              "`reset`",
              "exit, back to branch"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Bad test = bad bisect",
          "text": "Flaky or environment-dependent tests make bisection lie. Reproduce manually at the culprit, then verify with `git show`."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Beyond Bugs",
          "items": [
            "perf regressions: bad = slower",
            "any good/bad measurable property"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Scale check",
          "text": "log2(1000) ≈ 10 tests to pinpoint the culprit among a thousand commits."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pickaxe -S vs -G",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "`-S`",
            "`-G`"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Matches",
              "count change",
              "diff lines"
            ],
            [
              "Arg",
              "string",
              "regex"
            ],
            [
              "Speed",
              "faster",
              "slower"
            ],
            [
              "Precision",
              "coarse",
              "exact"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`-S` fires when the occurrence count of a string changes. `-G` fires when a changed line matches a regex."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git log -S'oldFn' --oneline",
            "git log -S'timeout=30' -- config/",
            "git log -G'req.*retry' --pickaxe-all"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--pickaxe-regex` treats `-S` arg as regex",
            "classic use: trace an API rename",
            "introduction AND removal commits both show"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bounding the Hunt",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "searches full history by default",
            "add `--since` or `v1.0..HEAD`",
            "pair with pathspec to cut cost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "-S sees",
                "lines": [
                  "string added",
                  "string removed"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "-S misses",
                "lines": [
                  "context edits",
                  "count unchanged"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Pickaxe: -S and -G Content Archaeology",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Invisible to -S",
          "text": "A commit editing surrounding lines but keeping the string count identical won't appear. Reach for `-G` there."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Found the SHA — what changed?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Read the commit per file"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "git show <sha> -- src/config.py"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "git reflog",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every HEAD move is recorded: commits, resets, rebases, checkouts. Kept 90 days, 30 for unreachable."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git reflog",
            "git reset --hard HEAD@{2}",
            "git checkout -b rescue <sha>",
            "git branch feat-x <sha>"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "nothing is lost until gc prunes reflog",
            "`HEAD@{n}` = n moves ago",
            "`HEAD@{'2 hours ago'}` = by time",
            "`branch@{n}` = that branch's own log"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "reset",
              "orphan",
              "reflog",
              "reset --hard",
              "reattached"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Recovery Kit",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "deleted branch → `git branch name <sha>`",
            "rebase botched → entry `rebase (start)`",
            "post-expiry → `git fsck --lost-found`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "bad reset",
              "`HEAD@{n}`"
            ],
            [
              "bad rebase",
              "`rebase (start)`"
            ],
            [
              "deleted branch",
              "branch at SHA"
            ],
            [
              "expired reflog",
              "`fsck`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Commits only",
          "text": "Reflog never recovers uncommitted work — that was never in a commit. Try IDE local history or swapfiles."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Limits & Habits",
          "items": [
            "reflog is local-only, never pushed",
            "can't save a teammate's lost commits",
            "`--autostash` or backup branch first",
            "`gc.reflogExpire` sets retention"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Decision Table",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Question",
            "Tool"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "broke the build?",
              "bisect"
            ],
            [
              "wrote this line?",
              "blame"
            ],
            [
              "symbol appeared?",
              "`-S`"
            ],
            [
              "lines matching X?",
              "`-G`"
            ],
            [
              "commit went where?",
              "reflog"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cost vs Precision",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Cost",
            "Precision"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`--grep`",
              "cheapest",
              "message-dependent"
            ],
            [
              "`-S`",
              "fast",
              "count-based"
            ],
            [
              "`-G`",
              "slower",
              "regex-exact"
            ],
            [
              "`blame -C`",
              "slow",
              "deepest"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Comparisons, Trade-offs, Common Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "bisect cost = the test runs, O(log n)",
            "blame walks full file history",
            "`-S`/`-G` scan every diff in range"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Top Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "stopping at the reformat blame",
            "forgetting `bisect reset` → detached HEAD",
            "flaky test bisects lie",
            "`HEAD@{n}` ≠ `HEAD~n`",
            "unbounded pickaxe scans for minutes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "HEAD@{2}",
                "lines": [
                  "reflog",
                  "local only"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "HEAD~2",
                "lines": [
                  "parent chain",
                  "pushed"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Per-clone reality",
          "text": "Reflog and blame don't survive someone's rebase-and-force-push on another machine. Reflog is per-clone."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Habits",
          "items": [
            "alias `pl = log --oneline --graph --all`",
            "keep `.git-blame-ignore-revs`",
            "bound pickaxe with pathspec"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Pick by question",
          "text": "Choose the tool from the question you're asking, not from muscle memory."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Regression Hunt",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Step 1: reproduce, write failing check",
            "Step 2: `bisect run` pins the SHA",
            "Step 3: `show` + `blame -w -C -L` for context",
            "Step 4: `-S` + `-p -L` for related history",
            "Step 5: botched rebase → reflog rescue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git bisect start HEAD v2.1",
            "git bisect run ./repro.sh",
            "git show <sha>; git blame -w -C -L",
            "git log -S'old_symbol'",
            "git reset --hard HEAD@{2}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Who Answers What",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Question",
            "Tool"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "WHERE",
              "bisect"
            ],
            [
              "WHEN/WHO",
              "blame, `-S`"
            ],
            [
              "HOW evolved",
              "`-G`, `-L`"
            ],
            [
              "WHAT happened",
              "reflog"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "The 6 commands to memorize?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`bisect run`",
            "`blame -w -C`",
            "`log -S`",
            "`log -G`",
            "`log -L`",
            "reflog + `reset --hard`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Prevention",
          "text": "Small commits, meaningful messages, tags on releases — every archaeology tool gets sharper on clean history."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Lost is rarely permanent",
          "text": "History is append-mostly and reflogged. With these five tools, almost nothing is truly gone."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "“It broke somewhere in the last 2,000 commits” is not a search strategy. This handbook turns Git history into a searchable, bisectable, recoverable dataset — one tool per question. Save it before your next mystery bug.",
